B.QN=s(['`differenceInDays` was off by one across a 23-hour DST day, which also made `calendar()` say "Today" instead of "Yesterday" or "Tomorrow".',"Weekday finders such as `nextMonday()` no longer drift by an hour across DST. `clone()`, `startOf`/`endOf` and the hour and minute finders return the right instant during a repeated fall-back hour.","`IsoWeekTimeRange.next`/`last` no longer get stuck or skip a week at DST, `LocalWeekTimeRange.next`/`last` keep `weekStart`, and `HourTimeRange.last` no longer sticks at spring-forward.","`TimeRange.encodeShort()` and `parse` keep UTC and `weekStart`; old strings still parse the same.",'Durations round before splitting into units, so 59m59.6s is one hour, not "59 minutes 60 seconds". Relative thresholds compare the rounded value, like moment.js.',"`fromPrecise(dropPrefixOrSuffix: true)` and `fromNowPrecise` honor the flag.","`Moment.maxValue` and `minValue` are the same instants as their UTC versions in every timezone.",'`byLocale` ignores case, and `byLanguage("e")` no longer matches `en`.',"`format()` is about 40% faster."],t.s)
B.Hb=new A.j1(B.QN,!1)
B.Sd=s(["On a `DateTime`, it defaults to the week start of the global localization. On this site, that's the language picked in the header.","On a `Moment`, it defaults to the moment's own localization.","`startOfIsoWeek()` always starts on Monday."],t.s)
B.Hc=new A.j1(B.Sd,!1)
B.SF=s(["On a `DateTime`, `weekStart` is optional and defaults to the global localization's week start. On this site, that's the language picked in the header.","On a `Moment`, the method takes no `weekStart`; it uses the moment's localization.","For ISO weeks, pass `DateTime.monday`, or compare `week` and `weekYear`."],t.s)
B.Hd=new A.j1(B.SF,!1)
B.U1=s(["Days the localization has a word for use that word: today, yesterday and tomorrow, and in some languages the day before yesterday and the day after tomorrow.",'1 to 6 days back is "last <weekday>", and 1 to 6 days ahead is the weekday name.',"7 or more days away is a date in the `l` format, with the time left out."],t.s)
B.He=new A.j1(B.U1,!1)
B.RD=s(["[Getters and operators](/extension/generic): `isLeapYear`, `quarter`, ISO `week`, `differenceInDays`, `clone()`, `format()`, and `<`, `>`, `+`, `-` on dates.","[Start of a unit](/extension/startOf): `startOfDay()`, `startOfLocalWeek()`, `startOf(DurationUnit.month)` and the rest.","[End of a unit](/extension/endOf): the last microsecond of a day, week, month or year.","[Next and last units](/extension/relativeFinders): `startOfNextMonth()`, `endOfLastLocalWeek()` and the other neighbors.","[Finding weekdays](/extension/findWeekday): `nextMonday()`, `lastFriday()`, `nextWeekday(n)`.","[Comparing units](/extension/isAtSame): `isAtSameDayAs()` and friends, which changed in 6.0.","[Clamped setters](/extension/set-clamped): set a day or month without spilling into the next one."],t.s)
B.Hf=new A.j1(B.RD,!1)
B.U5=s(["[Formatting](/formatting): every token, and the locale-aware formats like `LL` and `LT`.",'[Relative durations](/duration): "3 hours ago", "in a few seconds".',"[Time ranges](/time-range): this month, last week, and spans you can page through.","[Upgrading to 6.0](/upgrading): what changed, if you're coming from 5.x."],t.s)
B.Hg=new A.j1(B.U5,!1)
B.RY=s(["`d` and `e` both run 1 to 7 with Monday as 1, like `DateTime.weekday`. In moment.js `d` runs 0 to 6.",'The ordinal weekday is `d_o`, because `do` is a Dart keyword and can\'t name the enum value. In a pattern, `do` prints `d` followed by the letter "o".',"`YY` and `gg` give two digits only for 1970 through 2030 and print other years in full, so the short form can't be misread.","`w`, `ww`, `wo`, `gg` and `gggg` use ISO 8601 weeks, which start on Monday. A date in late December can be in week 1 of the next week year.","`ZZZ` is whatever `DateTime.timeZoneName` returns, which differs between platforms and browsers. Use `Z` or `ZZ` when the output has to be stable.",'Ordinals, month and weekday names, AM/PM, eras and the `L\u2026` formats come from the localization. A [custom localization](/creating-localization) that leaves one out prints a readable fallback such as "Day 65 of the year (ordered)".'],t.s)
B.Hh=new A.j1(B.RY,!1)
B.SO=s(["Replace assignments to `Moment.epoch`, `maxValue`, `minValue` and their `Utc` versions with your own variable.","Rename `CalenderLocalizationData` to `CalendarLocalizationData`, and every other `Calender\u2026` / `calender\u2026` name to `Calendar\u2026` / `calendar\u2026`.","If you used `isAtSame\u2026As` to compare wall-clock fields of dates in different timezones, convert both dates yourself first, or pass `enforceUTC: true`.","Where `to` can be before `from`, check before calling `CustomTimeRange(from, to)`, or use `from.rangeTo(to)`, which swaps them.","If you relied on `byLocale` returning `null` for an unsupported locale, call `byLocale(code, strict: true)`.","If you modified `localization.formatters`, write a [custom localization](/creating-localization) instead.","Update tests that compare localized output; many strings changed."],t.s)
B.Hi=new A.j1(B.SO,!0)
B.Uh=s(["Constructors: `Moment(date, localization: ...)`, `Moment.now`, `Moment.fromMillisecondsSinceEpoch`, `Moment.parse` and the rest.","`date.toMoment(localization: ...)` on any `DateTime`.","`moment.copyWith(localization: ...)` to switch an existing moment.",'`date.format(payload: "LL", localization: ...)` for a one-off string from a plain `DateTime`.',"`Moment.duration(duration, localization: ...)` and `duration.toDurationString(localization: ...)`.","`range.format(localization: ...)` on a [time range](/time-range)."],t.s)
